Project Overview & Vision
This repository documents the architecture, configuration, security monitoring, and threat emulation of a multi-subnet corporate virtual network built inside VMware Workstation Pro on a Kali Linux host.

The objective of this project is to bridge classroom theory and real-world production IT environments by simulating:

Network Defense & Routing: Stateful firewall filtering, DHCP authority, and double-NAT subnets.

Identity & Access Management: Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS), Group Policy Objects (GPOs), and local DNS resolution.

Threat Telemetry & Detection: Endpoint process tracking via Sysmon and centralized log ingestion via Wazuh SIEM.

Offensive Security & Emulation: Isolated DMZ target subnets for vulnerability scanning and attack simulation without risking corporate infrastructure.

